# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in. Never commit real values.
#
# psychology-mcp is the API layer — credentials live HERE, not in the plugin
# layer. A plugin declares MCP servers by URL and reaches credentials through
# ${VAR} expansion, headersHelper, or userConfig/sensitive; it never holds a key.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Polite-pool contact. Crossref and OpenAlex both grant materially better
# throughput when a contact address is present in the User-Agent. Both ran
# keyless at ~6.6 req/s with zero 429s during Layer-1 discovery.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PSYCHOLOGY_MCP_CONTACT_EMAIL=you@example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Semantic Scholar. Sent as the `x-api-key` request header.
#
# MEASURED 2026-08-15: the granted limit is 1 request/second CUMULATIVE across
# all endpoints. Pace UNDER it, as the issuer instructs — 1.3s spacing still
# drew a 429 in practice, so 2.5s is the observed-safe interval for sustained
# sequential use.
#
# Without a key the shared unauthenticated pool is unusable: zero of twelve
# benchmark queries completed across three observation windows spanning ~1.5h.
#
# ATTRIBUTION IS REQUIRED by the license agreement — any published material
# using S2 results must credit Semantic Scholar or cite "The Semantic Scholar
# Open Data Platform". This is a hard obligation, not a courtesy.
#
# Request a key: https://www.semanticscholar.org/product/api#api-key-form
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
S2_API_KEY=s2k-REPLACE_ME
